  "notes": "Singer-songwriter-turned-producer building band-tracked 1970s-facing pop. The documented method is the whole drum block: \"a real kit tracked in a non-studio room is the documented method (the furniture removed from a TV room and a kit put in it); soft-shouldered backbeat, room reverb, tambourine and shaker doubling, no grid-quantised hats.\" So `quantizeStrength` is 0.68 with double-digit jitter on every lane, the snare is `soft` transient under a `large` room tail, `hihat.continuous` is true with a wide velocity spread and no roll vocabulary at all, and `tambourine` and `shaker` double at `downbeat`. The bass is the second signature and the entry says it can be the hook: \"played electric bass running 8th-note melodic lines that outline chord tones — on several records the bass is the hook\", which is `independent_riff` at `followRootsProb` 0.3 with a chord-tone cell set and a full passing-tone list; no `bass808` block, because the entry says \"no 808\". Harmony is \"guitar-and-piano diatonic harmony with 7ths and a borrowed minor iv\" and \"harmony serves the topline and rarely modulates\", so the families are plain, `borrowed` carries the iv and `switchUpProb` stays low. The counter is the documented \"Rob Moose-style violin/viola string lines\", which is `sustain_pad` first with `answer_lick` behind it, entering on the second chorus per the arrangement note. ⚠ `confidence` is medium against a high-medium rating because the drum and harmonic numbers are INFERRED — the research documents a room, an instrument list and dated credits, not a pattern. `bpm.mode` 110 is the midpoint of the stated 90—130 band.",
